class PlaceableFilter(BaseModel):
    """A `placeableIn` question: the destination space, and the narrowing of it. Placeable means *affinely* placeable -- reaching the space across steps that compose into one affine map. A spike train or an irregularly sampled signal reaches its clock through a FIELD and is therefore not in this set, although an experiment view over it can still be created: a timeline can draw spike times without a matrix. This filter answers 'what can I lay out with one map', not 'what can I show'"""
    space: ID = Field(description='The space to be placed into. A *space*, not an experiment: every experiment over one world offers the same candidates. Pass `experiment.world.id` to ask it of an experiment')
    derived_only: bool | None = Field(validation_alias=AliasChoices('derived_only', 'derivedOnly'), serialization_alias='derivedOnly', default=None, description="Keep only what *needed* a lineage tree to get here: the filtered, decimated and sorted datasets placed by an ancestor's registration. What the space registers directly is dropped")
    require_affine: bool | None = Field(validation_alias=AliasChoices('require_affine', 'requireAffine'), serialization_alias='requireAffine', default=None, description='(elektro) Set false to ask *what is in this space* rather than *what can be drawn in it*: also admit what reaches it across a FIELD -- a variable-step run timed onto its clock by a lookup, a spike train. What is in a session is what is placed onto its clock; a picker keeps the strict default, which only offers what one affine map can draw')
    model_config = ConfigDict(extra='forbid', validate_assignment=True)

